# Version bump on every commit

Every commit in this repo must increment `package.json` `version` (semver patch by default, e.g. `2.0.3` → `2.0.4`).

The UI shows this version on the login screen and in the app header (`AppVersion` / `__APP_VERSION__` from Vite). Use it to confirm a deploy landed.

When committing:
1. Bump `package.json` version in the same change (or as part of the commit).
2. Do not skip the bump for “docs-only” or tiny fixes — every commit that ships to `main` needs a new version.
3. Mention the new version in the commit message when practical (e.g. `… (v2.0.4)`).
